/-!
# `A(V₃⁺)` is generated by its top level as an `A(V₀⁺)`-bimodule

For `V = V₀⁺` (`V0P`) and `M = V₃⁺` (`MV3`, lowest weight 2):

`bimodGen_V3`: every subspace `S ⊆ M` that contains `O(M)` (all `fzCirc`), contains
`M₂`, and is closed under `a ∗ ·` (`fzLeft`) and `· ∗ a` (`fzRight`) for all homogeneous
`a ∈ V`, is all of `M`.

Hence `A(M) = M/O(M)` is generated by the image of `M₂` as an `A(V)`-bimodule, for any
construction of `A(M)` whose `O(M)` and actions are given on homogeneous `a` by the standard
Frenkel–Zhu residues (`FZGenFiltration.lean`).

Proof: the criterion `FZGen.eq_top_of_lowerSpanM` reduces it to `V3_lowerSpanned`: for
`n ≥ 3`, `M_n` is spanned by the products `a₍ⱼ₎x`, `j ≤ 0`, `a ∈ V_p`, `x ∈ M_q`, `q < n`,
`p + q − j − 1 = n`.  By `V3_le_span_words` it suffices to treat word states `P(word ⊗ e^ν)`,
`ν ∈ Λ ∖ Λ₀`:

* **excited** (at least one oscillator): `excV3_mem_span` (`FZGenV3Sectors.lean`);
* **ground** `x_ν = e^ν + e^{-ν}`, `|ν|² = 2n ≥ 6` (`ground_mem_span`), by the **pair lemma**
  `exists_pair_gamma`: in Leech coordinates `x = lv ν` (all entries odd, `⟨μ,ν⟩ = lv μ·lv ν/8`),
  some `γ = 4(±eᵢ ± e_k) ∈ Λ₀` has `⟨γ,ν⟩ = (|xᵢ|+|x_k|)/2 = 3` or `≥ 5`
  (`exists_good_pair`: if every pair had `|xᵢ|+|x_k| ∈ {2,4,8}`, the largest entry would force
  `x = (m, ±1²³)` with `m ∈ {1,3,7}`, i.e. `|ν|² ∈ {3,4,9}`).  With `δ = ν − γ` and
  `f = ⟨γ,δ⟩ = ⟨γ,ν⟩ − 4`: `f = −1` gives `x_γ₍₀₎x_δ = ε·x_ν`; `f = k ≥ 1` gives
  `x_γ₍₋ₖ₋₁₎x_δ = ε·(x_ν + 2P(S_{2k}(γ) ⊗ e^{γ−δ}))`, whose second term is excited.

## Main results
* `exists_good_pair`, `exists_pair_gamma`, `ground_mem_span`.
* `V3_lowerSpanned`, `bimodGen_V3`.

## Status
`sorry`-free; no project axiom; unconditional (no hypotheses beyond the closure properties of
`S`); `#print axioms bimodGen_V3 = [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`.  Compatibility with
`Modules/FZBimodule.lean` (`FZ.fzO`, `FZ.fzLeft`, `FZ.fzRight`) is `FZGenBridge.lean`
(`fzGenerated_MV3 : FZ.FZGenerated MV3 2`).  Only the closure of `S` is used: the `A(V)`-bimodule
structure on `M/O(M)` itself (`O(V) ∗ M ⊆ O(M)` etc.) is not needed and not proved.  Imported by the
umbrella `VOA/Moonshine.lean`.
-/

set_option linter.style.longLine false
set_option linter.unusedSimpArgs false

